WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.560
There are lots of good reasons
to try and follow a healthier diet—

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.640
you lose weight,
you feel good,

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.440
but the main reason?

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.000
To live a longer, happier,
more productive life.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.040
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.760
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.040
Today we look at some of the
ways to reduce wrinkles.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.200
And we start with a look
at the safety and efficacy

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.341
of botox injections
and facelift surgery.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.120
Anti-aging medicine
is one of the fastest growing

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.520
medical specialties,
and often targeted at women,

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.880
who are urged to restore
their youthful appearance

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.680
by "any and all
available means."

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:40.720
This includes surgery.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.840
92 percent
of cosmetic procedures

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.920
are performed on women,
most commonly Botox, fillers,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.400
and laser or chemical
peel skin resurfacing,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.960
but millions in the U.S. undergo
cosmetic surgery every year,

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.760
including hundreds of thousands
of face-lifts.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.160
There's no consensus on
the best face-lift technique.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.400
None have been shown to be
definitively better than others.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.080
A systematic review found that
most of the studies

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.480
on the newest techniques
were mere case series,

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.640
one of the lowest levels
on the hierarchy of evidence,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.760
basically composed of a string
of glorified anecdotes.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.080
According to one of the largest
and most up-to-date analyses,

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.040
face-lifts are considered
relatively safe when performed

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.720
by a board-certified
plastic surgeon,

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.640
with surgical complications
only happening

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.960
in about 1 in 20 cases,
most often hematomas,

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.200
where blood collects
under the skin flaps,

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.520
or minor infections.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.560
Serious infections,

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.040
like facial necrotizing
fasciitis

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.880
caused by flesh-eating bacteria
are rare,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.600
as is pyoderma gangrenosum,

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.040
a disfiguring, skin ulcerating
autoimmune disease

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.792
that can be triggered
by face-lift surgery.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.160
Nerve injuries occur in at most
a few percent of cases,

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.600
but only about
1 in 1000 procedures

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:59.960
may result in permanent
facial nerve injury.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.320
About two-thirds of face-lifts

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.600
are performed under
general anesthesia,

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.920
which is associated with
a greater risk of complications.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.160
The most important way
to mediate risk

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.840
is to refrain from smoking.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.920
Smoking can increase the risk
of skin flap necrosis,

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.000
or tissue death,
up to twenty-fold.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.840
Patients should refrain from
smoking at least a month before

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.960
and month after surgery.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.600
Tempering expectations
is also important.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.120
Approximately 1 in 3 women

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.920
experience a period
of postoperative depression,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.640
but this may just be
in reaction to

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.080
the temporary distortion
and discoloration

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.760
of swelling and bruising
after surgery.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:42.520
The most profitable
cosmetic procedure is Botox,

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.280
in the billions,

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.960
as well as the most common,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:50.000
performed more than four million
times a year in the US alone.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.040
It all started when
a group of surgeons noticed

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.040
that patients with Bell's palsy,
facial paralysis,

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.840
didn't have as many wrinkles.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.720
So what about
injecting minute amounts

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.920
of the nerve-blocking toxin
that causes botulism

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.200
to paralyze a few
facial muscles on purpose,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.640
and a multibillion-dollar
industry was born.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:12.960
The effect is temporary,

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.120
typically lasting
three to four months

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.480
until the body can grow back
new nerve terminals.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.760
In response to cases of
respiratory failure and death

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.480
occurring hours or even weeks
after injection,

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:27.880
in 2009 the FDA mandated
a black box warning

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.040
regarding the potential
spread of the toxin

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:30.960
resulting in death

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.920
from swallowing
and breathing difficulties

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:37.200
occurring hours, days,
or weeks after injection.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.520
However, most of these
complications were tied

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.440
not to cosmetic uses
but to treating muscle spasms--

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.760
for example in cerebral palsy.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:50.120
For wrinkles, only 30 to 60
units of the toxin may be used,

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.560
compared to an average of about
180 for severe muscle spasms,

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.000
though still a far cry
from the estimated lethal dose

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.000
of perhaps 3,000 units.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.560
The dose is given in MU,
"mouse units,"

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:06.440
with one MU being the amount
capable of poisoning

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:09.680
half of a group
of albino mice to death.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.800
In studies, less than
1 in 2,000 Botox procedures

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.400
resulted in complications,

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.720
which can include droopy
eyelids, double vision,

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:23.160
an asymmetrical smile,
or the Spock,

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.480
a devilish curvature of
the outer portion of the brow.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.360
Unfortunately, not all such
procedures are performed

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.080
under such
controlled conditions.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.600
In many states,
there is surprisingly little

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.720
or no regulation
as to who can deliver Botox,

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:39.800
leading to a rapid increase
in injections

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.080
by nonmedical personnel.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.880
In one five-ish year period,

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.720
about 30,000 complications
allegedly tied to Botox

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.320
were reported to the FDA,

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:54.200
most commonly pain, swelling,
and eyelid or eyebrow drooping,

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.120
but most adverse effects are
transient and self-limited.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.160
In our next story,

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:04.720
almonds are put to the test in a randomized
controlled trial for facial wrinkles.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.400
After my video on dates
blew my mind, showing that

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.000
eating just a few dates
can significantly reduce

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.440
the duration of labor
during childbirth and

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:15.409
improve the progression of labor.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.920
But there are some surprising
benefits attributed to nuts

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.840
in randomized controlled
trials, like how about a study

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.120
on the effects of almond
consumption on wrinkles?

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.720
Where’d they even
come up with the idea?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.240
Well, population studies
have found that healthy diets

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.440
are associated with
less facial wrinkles,

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.320
like a meat and junk-
predominant eating pattern

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.360
was associated with
more wrinkles, whereas

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.760
a fruit-predominant pattern was
associated with fewer wrinkles.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:44.200
In terms of single foods,
yellow vegetables and soy

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:47.440
appear protective, but
wine may make things worse.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:49.600
Their thinking is that it
might be the antioxidants

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.640
in healthy foods decreasing
the oxidative stress load,

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:56.560
or the anti-inflammatory benefits,
or protection from sun damage,

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.640
or improved collagen production,
or better DNA repair.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:00.240
I have videos on most
of those topics.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.920
The bottom line is
that eating healthier

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:05.080
may reduce wrinkling, which
could actually save lives

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.160
if people started eating healthier

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.760
to maintain a more youthful
appearance and get all

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:13.680
the chronic disease benefits
as a happy side effect.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.920
Other studies have found the same
thing, supporting recommendations

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.440
for more healthy foods like
fruits, vegetables, and nuts.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.160
Here’s another
study that landed on

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.960
yellow vegetables,
and greens as well.

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:27.840
In this study, a high intake of
vegetables, beans, and olive oil

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.160
appeared to be protective against

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.560
spots of precancerous
sun damage,

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:35.240
whereas a high intake of meat
and dairy may make things worse.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:39.040
Prunes, apples, and tea
seemed particularly good,

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.080
but this was a
cross-sectional study,

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.080
meaning just a snapshot in time.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:46.200
Maybe people who eat more meat
are out barbequing in the sun,

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:50.360
or people who eat more prunes
just use more sunblock.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:53.640
You can’t know for sure if
foods actually affect wrinkling

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.360
until you... put them to the test—

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:01.600
but we had no such
studies…until, now.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.440
Why study almonds?

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:06.720
Because it was paid for by
the Almond Board, of course.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.840
The researchers didn’t know
who was in the nut group, though,

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.520
and who was in
the control group,

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.800
until they were
looking at the results.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.720
The nut group were given
2 ounces of nuts a day,

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.640
like two palmfuls of nuts, and
the control group was instead

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:21.760
given nut-free snacks
to eat instead

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.760
like nut-free granola
bars or pretzels.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:28.640
Before and after, they got
high‐res facial photographs

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.600
to quantify facial wrinkle
depth and severity using

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:37.000
a computer‐based photographic
analysis and…boom,

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.000
the almond group had significantly
decreased wrinkle severity

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:45.960
compared with the control group
by the end of the 16-week study.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.040
The paper concludes:
“Our study demonstrates that

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:52.160
daily almond consumption
may reduce wrinkle severity...”

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:55.240
Now, they used a relatively
large dose, 2 ounces a day,

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.560
whereas you can get
cardioprotective benefits

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.160
of nuts from even less
than a half an ounce;

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.280
so, who knows, maybe they could
have gotten away with using less.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.760
Here’s the low-dose nut
study they referenced,

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:09.040
showing a significant drop in
LDL cholesterol within 6 weeks

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.640
eating just a few
almonds a day—10 grams

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.600
which is just like
8 almonds a day.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.480
That’s the nice thing
about healthy foods,

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:18.680
they just have good
side effects.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.960
So, global disease prevention
strategies might beneﬁt

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:25.080
from emphasizing that a
healthy diet is also linked

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:29.080
to less facial wrinkling,
and maybe vanity will help us

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:33.680
prevent a few heart
attacks in the bargain.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:34.640
Finally today,

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:39.240
did you know that the skin folding
caused by everyday facial expressions

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:44.200
etches once-temporary grooves
into permanent wrinkles,

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:49.661
but only in the context of
underlying structural damage.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.280
How are wrinkles formed?

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.720
Their origin and nature is said
to be "notoriously complex,"

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.760
but current thinking
is that wrinkles occur

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.960
where fault lines
develop in aging skin.

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:04.840
The process has been compared
to an old leather glove,

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:06.320
made out of skin after all,

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.920
that develops creases
at the joints

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:10.560
due to repetitive stress.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:12.720
In the face,
the repeated flexion

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:14.920
may be due
to facial expression.

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.680
An 8-year longitudinal study

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.560
found that you can predict
the pattern

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.480
of persistent wrinkles

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:23.280
by superimposing
upon your resting face

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:26.040
the expression lines,
temporary wrinkles,

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:28.000
that form when you smile.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.040
Over time,
the skin folding

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.120
caused by
everyday facial expressions

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.787
etches the temporary grooves
into permanent wrinkles.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:38.680
Given that wrinkles develop
from forehead furrows

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.360
and expression lines
from frowns and laughter,

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:44.000
one dermatology journal review
on aging skin

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.240
offered the tongue in
unwrinkled-cheek suggestion

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:52.000
of "Living alone to minimize
the use of facial expressions."

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:53.160
And while you're at it
you could

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.160
"live in space to avoid
the effects of gravity."

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:59.000
However, there is a way
to freeze parts of your face

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:03.080
into an expressionless mask:
Botox.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:06.440
In fact, one contraindication
to getting Botox

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:07.680
is having a job that

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:11.320
"necessitates a wide range
of facial expressions."

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.600
It's never been
formally put to the test,

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:17.120
but there was a case report
of a pair of identical twins,

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.160
one of whom who spent
tens of thousands of dollars

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:23.120
getting Botox treatments across
multiple areas on her face

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.640
a few times each year
for 13 years.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.680
Compared to her
non-regularly injected twin,

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:32.040
she ended up with
fewer imprinted facial lines.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.400
A paper entitled
"Sleep Wrinkles"

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.480
tried to make the case
that wrinkles may result

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:39.680
from the skin distortion
from mechanical compression

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:41.920
sleeping on your side.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.960
Of course, the primary author
also is a partner in a company

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:49.800
selling $160 quote-unquote
"wrinkle-fighting" pillows.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:52.640
It turns out there does not
appear to be any correlation

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.480
between sleep position
preference

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.280
and the appearance of wrinkles.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.640
Speaking of
questionable products,

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:02.360
what about topical adhesive
"anti-wrinkle" pads

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.880
you paste to your face at night?

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:08.640
Product claims include "look up
to 10-15 years younger,"

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.560
declaring a 70 percent reduction
in wrinkles.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.280
But when actually
put to the test for a month

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:18.520
for crow's feet, forehead,
or between-the-eye wrinkles,

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:22.680
no objective benefits
were reported at all.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:26.120
There did appear to be a placebo
effect in that subjectively,

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:28.600
the study participants felt
the wrinkles looked better,

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:30.880
but independent
blinded evaluations

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:33.600
by facial plastic surgeons
of before-and-after pictures

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:37.320
showed no significant change.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:40.600
So what can we do
to prevent wrinkling?

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:42.240
Some of it is genetics.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:46.000
For example, having lighter skin
color is a predisposing factor.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.680
Among light skin tones,

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:51.600
Caucasian skin wrinkles more
readily than Asian skin,

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.480
for which aging
is more characterized

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:54.920
by pigmentation changes

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:58.440
such as freckles, blotchy
patches, and liver spots.

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.080
Among Asian skin types,

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:02.520
Chinese women tend to have
more wrinkles around their eyes

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.440
than Japanese women,

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:05.320
whereas Thai women
tend to wrinkle more

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.880
in the lower half
of their faces.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:11.280
There are, however,
factors we have control over.

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:14.760
For example, drier skin has
also been found predictive

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:16.440
of more persistent wrinkling,

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:21.120
suggesting regular use
of skin moisturizers may help.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.520
When it comes
to wrinkle formation,

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:25.800
it takes two to tango.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:28.040
Wrinkles are formed
by repetitive creasing

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:30.400
of aged skin.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:32.520
Kids can scrunch their faces
all they want

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:34.960
because the architecture
of their skin has yet to be

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.560
irreparably damaged,

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.880
and the lack of creasing

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:40.320
is why you don't have
wrinkles on your forearms

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:43.520
no matter how much sun
they've soaked up.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.760
Rather than immobilizing
your face with Botox,

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:50.240
you can focus on preventing
the underlying structural damage

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.360
that makes your skin
susceptible.

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:57.040
This involves tobacco avoidance
and regular sun protection.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:01.120
What about safeguarding
against other kinds of light?

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:04.000
From the Journal of Biomedical
Physics and Engineering:

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.320
"Can light emitted
from smartphone screens

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:12.160
and taking selfies cause
premature aging and wrinkles?"

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:16.360
Human skin cells bathed in
the light of iPhones and iPads

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:19.760
experienced an 80 to 90 percent
increase in free radicals,

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:22.000
compared to shielded
control cells,

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.240
suggesting electronic device
generated light

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.880
"may be harmful to skin."

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:30.840
Now, on one hand,
they positioned the screens

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:34.080
unrealistically close,
one centimeter,

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.360
resulting in about
10 times the irradiance

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:39.360
compared to a reading distance
of about a foot.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.640
On the other hand,
the skin cells were only exposed

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:45.760
for an unrealistically
short time, only an hour.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.240
The researchers called
for future studies

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.280
to evaluate the impact
of lower, longer doses

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:54.920
on skin outcomes
such as collagen deposition.

